  "text": "# The Sum of the First n Cubes: A Complete Derivation, Induction Proof, and Numerical Verification\n\n## Part 1: Derivation from First Principles\n\nWe seek a closed form for the sum of the first $n$ cubes:\n\n$$S_n = \\sum_{k=1}^{n} k^3 = 1^3 + 2^3 + 3^3 + \\cdots + n^3$$\n\n### 1.1 The Key Insight: Telescoping via a Cubic Antiderivative\n\nThe most natural \"first principles\" approach is to find a polynomial $F(k)$ whose *finite difference* produces $k^3$. That is, we want:\n\n$$F(k) - F(k-1) = k^3$$\n\nIf such an $F$ exists, then summing over $k = 1, 2, \\ldots, n$ gives a",
